	affiliations = {Northeastern University, Boston, United States},
	abstract = {This paper presents Watchdog, an AI-assisted analysis tool designed to support journalists in uncovering narrative patterns, community sentiment, and systemic power dynamics across digital media platforms. Targeting transcripts, comments, and articles, the system integrates natural language processing (NLP), sentiment analysis, topic modeling, and multimodal visualizations to enhance journalistic storytelling. A user-facing interface enables exploration through interactive charts, word clouds, and audio-visual snapshots. Preliminary feedback from journalists in Mexico highlights the tool's usability and its potential to reduce the learning curve in data-driven reporting. Key contributions include interactive visualizations, a layered approach to topic modelling, a multimodal framework to present data, and sentiment analysis. The findings highlight the potential of computational tools to elevate underrepresented voices and enhance storytelling transparency. Future work includes broader user studies and integration of fact-checking features. © 2025 Elsevier B.V., All rights reserved.},
